Evaluator: A. Psaltis (04/2025)
Comments:
1. New resonance measurements since Iliadis et al. (2010): Dombos et al. (2022) and Wang et al. (2023) for resonances at Er= 388, 472, 543, 615 and 628 keV.
Bayesian weighted average has been applied to the aforementioned resonance strengths.
2. For resonances with Er>700 keV we are using the evaluated values of Iliadis et al. (2010)
3. Direct capture (E2) is estimated using (adopting) alpha spectroscopic factors from (6Li,d) experiment of Anantaraman et al. (1977).
The results are consistent with the direct capture from Iliadis et al. (2010), within a factor of 2.
